LOGBOOK.md:8:### 0732 — Extended lifecycle converges to a bounded HEV/runtime envelope (TASK-260715-135rr8)
LOGBOOK.md:9:- INVESTIGATION: A bounded process-local 2000-cycle SwiftPM/loopback run captured every physical-footprint jump and 100-cycle segment. The sampler observed both rises and releases, including `-1,196,032 B` and `-1,130,496 B` segments; post-warmup net change was `-2,310,120 B`. Across the last 500 samples, net change was `-65,536 B` and range was `98,304 B`. Descriptors stayed `3`, threads stayed within `6...8`, and every post-cleanup HEV session, read, and queue count was zero. Boundary start/stop and HEV start/main-return counters were exactly one per cycle. Earlier 500- and 1000-cycle repeats still had late rises, proving neither duration alone established convergence.
LOGBOOK.md:10:- RULE: The production evidence gate now requires at least 2000 samples (20× the original 100-cycle minimum), the existing fixed 10-sample allocator warmup, post-warmup and trailing 1000-sample maximum drawup no greater than `256 KiB` (1% of the upper 25 MiB provisional envelope), and either a trailing plateau or an observed post-warmup release. Maximum drawup measures each upward excursion from the running minimum, so a large release is not itself a failure. Raw evidence records every parameter, transition count, jump cycle, ownership counter, and sample. Positive plateau and bounded-oscillation tests plus unreleased late-rise and oversized-high-water negative tests bind the classifier; the original rise-plus-plateau negative remains.
LOGBOOK.md:13:### 0716 — Correct lifecycle trend gate stops rev3 matrix (TASK-260715-135rr8)
LOGBOOK.md:14:- FIX: The physical-matrix entry now independently computes the actual working candidate tree with a task-local temporary Git index and rejects a well-formed forged `RELUX_CANDIDATE_TREE_OID` before HEV work or evidence emission. It independently hashes the linked macOS HEV archive against the pinned manifest. Negative production-call-site coverage rejects forged tree and artifact hashes.
LOGBOOK.md:15:- RULE: Lifecycle analysis uses an explicit fixed 10-sample allocator warmup. Across the remaining 90 samples it classifies any non-decreasing sequence with at least one increase as monotonic growth and records warmup/window/net-change plus increase/equal/decrease transition counts. Pure negative coverage flags rise-plus-plateau and accepts a plateau stabilized after warmup.
LOGBOOK.md:16:- STOP: Three independent 100-cycle physical-Mac probes all failed the corrected gate: `+81,920 B` with `4/85/0`, `+81,920 B` with `5/84/0`, and `+98,328 B` with `4/85/0` increase/equal/decrease transitions. Per rev3 instructions, the 100/250/500 matrix and full suite were not run against a known failing lifecycle prerequisite, and the rule was not weakened. No VPN, NetworkExtension, route, DNS, interface, packet-filter, SSH, or global-memory-pressure operation ran.
LOGBOOK.md:20:- LIFECYCLE: One hundred real HEV start/traffic/stop cycles restored descriptors, sessions, queued batches, outstanding reads, boundary start/stop ownership, and HEV/bridge close stages; sampled physical footprint did not grow monotonically. Seven startup and seven cleanup cancellation stages plus 50 harness host-termination iterations passed.
