LOGBOOK.md:730:- RESOLVER/FAIRNESS: Domain use validates the accepted ASCII presentation form (including numeric-text and malformed A-label rejection) before a cancellable resolver seam. Concurrent requests, deadline, inspected result count, copied result bytes, family selection, turn targets, socket visits, datagrams, bytes, and monotonic time all have immutable checked caps. The inspected-result cap is independent of accepted results, so invalid resolver output cannot force an unbounded scan. Names, addresses, payloads, and raw resolver/socket errors never enter diagnostics or metric dimensions.
LOGBOOK.md:740:- IMPLEMENTATION: A single Go owner goroutine now linearizes relay association admission, descriptor use, activity, close, expiry, generation replacement, and cancellation. Identity is the session generation plus nonzero client association ID plus a monotonically increasing local incarnation, so stale timer/activity/close work cannot affect a reused numeric ID.
LOGBOOK.md:741:- RESOURCE POLICY: Association, family-specific socket, logical timer, and pending-close credits are checked before descriptor creation and report finite aggregate counters. One indexed deadline heap and one physical monotonic timer bound timer/task state; expiry events consume reserved pending-close credit until observed. IPv4 and IPv6 descriptors are created lazily and closed exactly once across normal, partial-failure, expiry, session, process, and cancellation paths.
LOGBOOK.md:743:- VERIFICATION: Pinned Go 1.26.5 focused tests passed 20 repeated runs and the race detector; targeted lifecycle tests passed 100 repeated runs; full relay tests, vet, and build passed. `make relay-protocol-check` passed schema/vector/drift checks and 57 protocol tests; the full Swift suite passed 318 tests and Swift build passed. Real descriptor tests prove IPv4/IPv6 family, `O_NONBLOCK`, `FD_CLOEXEC`, port zero, unconnected state, and post-close `EBADF`; board, formatting, diff, privacy, and resource scans are clean.
LOGBOOK.md:752:- FAIL-CLOSED RULE: Missing, duplicate, wrong-phase, wrong-tuple, or accidentally active relay work makes the degraded predicate false and projects no usable service. T14/T15/T19/T22 establish the target lifecycle plus exact prospective registration before re-evaluation and publication; race-test handoff covers positive and negative cases.
LOGBOOK.md:758:- PROJECTION/DIAGRAMS: Public Full/Degraded predicates are target-state truth rather than circular source guards. Reasserting and every candidate/validator phase remain all-false. The lifecycle diagram now distinguishes M3 Awaiting Base from registered Validating Relay; the ownership view remains authority-only.
LOGBOOK.md:762:- GENERATION: Relay timers, attempts, sessions, health/process/channel watchers, and association callbacks now require a non-null M2 relay-work registration with a monotonic work generation, attempt generation when applicable, and finite phase. Retirement clears that registration before cleanup, publication, or rescheduling, so a late callback from attempt N is stale even before N+1 exists.
