LOGBOOK.md:814:- DECISION: `TCPAdmissionRegistry` is one generation-scoped mutex authority for pending handshakes, authenticated flows, concurrent channel opens, owned channels, fixed directional queue capacity, live buffered bytes, and phase counts. All ceilings and the measured-safe/HEV evidence gates are caller-injected; denial is synchronous, retains no waiter, maps to SOCKS5 `REP=01`, and explicitly prohibits an SSH open. Reservation identifiers are monotonically allocated without reuse and fail closed with finite `identifier_capacity` pressure before `UInt64` wrap.
LOGBOOK.md:817:- VERIFICATION: Eighteen admission tests cover below/at/above every independent ceiling, 128/256-way reserve races, 500 release/open and 500 late-callback races, 250 explicit-release/deinit ownership races, ID exhaustion, queued-byte overflow, session-health races, 8,000 sustained pressure rejects alongside 2,000 admitted-flow progress steps, every terminal reason across 320 churn lifecycles, and exact local/exported baseline recovery. The bounded-queue convergence probe passes 20/20 runs; focused normal and TSan admission/diagnostics suites pass; `make validate-core` passes boundary/native gates, 306 tests in 27 suites, and the post-test build; strict recursive Swift format, privacy/boundary, diff, and board validation pass.
LOGBOOK.md:821:- CANCELLATION: One locked control signal wakes local readiness, cancels both structured child tasks, calls `SSHByteChannel.cancel()` once, discards late positive completions, joins both directions, and releases the aggregate reservation once. EOF, cancellation, local/remote closure, read/write error, zero progress, and bound violation are handed to the later lifecycle owner as finite directional events; the pump does not choose half-close/reset policy.
LOGBOOK.md:827:- BOUNDARY: Wrong/stale capability and the M1 monotonic accept-to-auth deadline remain authentication-phase failures with only phase-and-remaining-budget-safe replies. The post-handoff adapter resource reservation is separate from the boundary pending-authentication ceiling.
LOGBOOK.md:832:- CORRECTION: Current `HEVSOCKSBoundary` uses `SO_RCVTIMEO`, which is a per-receive inactivity bound and can restart as bytes arrive; authentication sends have no deadline. The pending set is count-bounded, but current source does not prove an absolute accept-to-auth deadline. M1 must compute one monotonic deadline at accept, apply its remaining budget across greeting/auth reads, comparisons, and replies without progress extension, and prove slow-trickle/reply-stall eviction plus slot/descriptor release on iOS and macOS.
LOGBOOK.md:849:- DECISION: `OwnedVPNManagerRepository` remains the only ownership/schema authority and now hands out a session only from a freshly loaded exact-owned current manager. `VPNSessionController` retains no manager cache or forwarding state; iOS/macOS wrappers retain the fresh manager only to keep its exact public `NETunnelProviderSession` alive for the command/observer lifetime.
LOGBOOK.md:850:- ORDERING: Start and stop share one locked once-only stop claim, so cancellation, timeout, and a concurrent explicit stop cannot duplicate `stopTunnel`. Controller retirement cancels host waits and observers without claiming that stop; a cancelled stop waiter does not cancel the joined system-stop observation for other callers.
LOGBOOK.md:851:- PROJECTION: Every non-connected system status clears capability immediately. A connected projection accepts only correlated, negotiated lifecycle/capability responses at one matching position strictly newer than the last accepted generation/sequence; relaunch starts without historical app state and asks the provider again. Non-running provider lifecycle states fail safe to zero capabilities.
LOGBOOK.md:853:- COVERAGE: Deterministic Swift Testing covers every status, exact v1 start options, synchronous errors, 60/15/3-second deadlines, cancellation/retirement, start-stop races, joined stops, initial observer races, deallocation, nil/late/wrong/corrupt/unsupported/mismatched/stale responses, generation reset, and app recreation.
LOGBOOK.md:857:- FIX: iOS and macOS now install the observer first and then perform an authoritative status read through an injectable seam. The locked retirement handshake also handles a synchronous terminal notification before registration returns its token: completion wins once, and the late-arriving token is immediately unregistered.
LOGBOOK.md:863:- FIX: Every public ensure/enable/disable/remove/repair entry point now crosses one FIFO operation gate, held through its terminal result; internal repair convergence reuses the held operation without re-entering the gate. Manager-contract inspection carries signed `Int` or unsigned `UInt64` versions without narrowing, while Boolean, fractional, and other type-confused versions fail closed with zero mutations.
LOGBOOK.md:886:### 0245 — VPN lifecycle separates ownership, enablement, system state, and runtime capability (TASK-260715-1q4qhw)
LOGBOOK.md:889:- AUTHORITY: `NETunnelProviderSession.status` is the sole system-session authority; a fresh generation/sequence provider snapshot is the sole runtime capability authority. Host suspension/termination removes observers only. Provider start/stop once-gates and exact deadlines remain extension-owned and join the accepted coordinator cleanup.
LOGBOOK.md:901:- FIX: The lifecycle now models one `generationConsumed` invariant shared by start and stop. A winning pre-start stop records termination, enters stopping, and runs the existing single cleanup owner; this releases the configuration reference before returning and makes every later start reject with `generationAlreadyConsumed`.
LOGBOOK.md:907:- FIX: After joining the startup child, `start()` now rechecks caller cancellation, environment cancellation, lifecycle ownership, and termination while actor-isolated before atomically clearing `startupTask` and returning. A callback that wins the handoff therefore forces the error/cleanup path; a callback that arrives after the atomic handoff observes no startup owner and starts cleanup itself.
LOGBOOK.md:927:- PRIVACY: The default schema has no lane/run/flow IDs, DNS or destination fields, addresses, credentials, commands/stdin, payload content, or traffic samples. State transition times are monotonic process-uptime milliseconds; errors retain only validated domain/code; flow, memory, route, health, packet/byte, drop-reason, DNS-result, and SSH values are aggregates.
