## 2026-08-27

### 0732 — Extended lifecycle converges to a bounded HEV/runtime envelope (TASK-260715-135rr8)
- INVESTIGATION: A bounded process-local 2000-cycle SwiftPM/loopback run captured every physical-footprint jump and 100-cycle segment. The sampler observed both rises and releases, including `-1,196,032 B` and `-1,130,496 B` segments; post-warmup net change was `-2,310,120 B`. Across the last 500 samples, net change was `-65,536 B` and range was `98,304 B`. Descriptors stayed `3`, threads stayed within `6...8`, and every post-cleanup HEV session, read, and queue count was zero. Boundary start/stop and HEV start/main-return counters were exactly one per cycle. Earlier 500- and 1000-cycle repeats still had late rises, proving neither duration alone established convergence.
- RULE: The production evidence gate now requires at least 2000 samples (20× the original 100-cycle minimum), the existing fixed 10-sample allocator warmup, post-warmup and trailing 1000-sample maximum drawup no greater than `256 KiB` (1% of the upper 25 MiB provisional envelope), and either a trailing plateau or an observed post-warmup release. Maximum drawup measures each upward excursion from the running minimum, so a large release is not itself a failure. Raw evidence records every parameter, transition count, jump cycle, ownership counter, and sample. Positive plateau and bounded-oscillation tests plus unreleased late-rise and oversized-high-water negative tests bind the classifier; the original rise-plus-plateau negative remains.
- ANOMALY/FIX: The first extended attempt stopped at cycle 257 with Swift signal 5 because the test payload used checked `UInt8(iteration)`. `UInt8(truncatingIfNeeded:)` removes that artificial 255-cycle harness limit while address and port continue to identify each flow. The 2000-cycle investigation passed in 106.74 seconds. No VPN, NetworkExtension, route, DNS, interface, packet-filter, SSH, or global-memory-pressure operation ran.

### 0716 — Correct lifecycle trend gate stops rev3 matrix (TASK-260715-135rr8)
- FIX: The physical-matrix entry now independently computes the actual working candidate tree with a task-local temporary Git index and rejects a well-formed forged `RELUX_CANDIDATE_TREE_OID` before HEV work or evidence emission. It independently hashes the linked macOS HEV archive against the pinned manifest. Negative production-call-site coverage rejects forged tree and artifact hashes.
- RULE: Lifecycle analysis uses an explicit fixed 10-sample allocator warmup. Across the remaining 90 samples it classifies any non-decreasing sequence with at least one increase as monotonic growth and records warmup/window/net-change plus increase/equal/decrease transition counts. Pure negative coverage flags rise-plus-plateau and accepts a plateau stabilized after warmup.
- STOP: Three independent 100-cycle physical-Mac probes all failed the corrected gate: `+81,920 B` with `4/85/0`, `+81,920 B` with `5/84/0`, and `+98,328 B` with `4/85/0` increase/equal/decrease transitions. Per rev3 instructions, the 100/250/500 matrix and full suite were not run against a known failing lifecycle prerequisite, and the rule was not weakened. No VPN, NetworkExtension, route, DNS, interface, packet-filter, SSH, or global-memory-pressure operation ran.

### 0625 — Physical HEV/bridge matrix meets the provisional incremental target (TASK-260715-135rr8)
- MEASUREMENT: A physical Mac15,9 (arm64, macOS 26.5) SwiftPM run admitted 100, 250, and the explicitly narrowed 500-session ceiling with zero bridge drops. Physical footprint was 12,354,160 B, 15,270,512 B, and 20,038,256 B; peak was 20,054,640 B. The incremental 500-session HEV/bridge cost was 11,976,704 B, leaving 19,480,576 B inside the provisional 30 MiB envelope. This is not a whole-extension Apple guarantee and does not allocate SSH, DNS, relay, caches, or reconnect overlap.
- LIFECYCLE: One hundred real HEV start/traffic/stop cycles restored descriptors, sessions, queued batches, outstanding reads, boundary start/stop ownership, and HEV/bridge close stages; sampled physical footprint did not grow monotonically. Seven startup and seven cleanup cancellation stages plus 50 harness host-termination iterations passed.
- AVAILABILITY: `os_proc_available_memory` is explicitly unavailable on macOS in the public SDK. HEV queued bytes and process-wide Swift task counts also have no public gauge. All are recorded as unavailable/unknown; host memory, process threads, and proxy zeros were not substituted. Physical iPhone and sleep/wake remain named deferred gaps.
- PRESSURE: Real stalled-path pressure accounts every send or bounded drop and cleans up. Soft/pressure/critical ordering remains deferred until SSH admission integration because the current memory-pressure seam is advisory and has no production policy consumer; no global pressure tool was invoked.
- VERIFICATION: The full Swift suite and full coverage suite each passed 480 tests in 40 suites with 25 declared known candidate-unavailable issues. Affected coverage is 84.84% regions, 96.02% functions, and 93.09% lines. Strict affected-file format lint and `git diff --check` pass. Raw matrix JSON and logs are attached as task-scoped evidence.
- REV2 AUTHENTICITY: Every final raw run is fail-closed on an exact candidate tree OID and reads the pinned HEV revision/source SHA-256 from `NativeDependencies/manifest.json`. Each emitting run performs and serializes its own 100-cycle descriptor/thread/session/read/queue/physical-footprint samples and derives monotonic growth from those values. The original signal 6 came from the retired `proc_pid_rusage` importer; the final sampler uses public `task_info(TASK_VM_INFO)` plus `proc_pidinfo(PROC_PIDTASKINFO)` and is exercised by three independent exact-tree runs.

### 2356 — Physical macOS MTU/socket baseline separates queue drops from send refusal (TASK-260715-gyg51r)
- MEASUREMENT: The bounded loopback-only SPM harness ran 36 rows on a physical Apple M3 Max Mac (arm64, macOS 26.5): MTU 1500/4096/8500 × IPv4/native IPv6/dual stack × nominal/constrained-buffer/25ms receiver-stall/mixed bidirectional traffic. Nominal and mixed rows delivered 100%; pressure rows produced only named bounded effects and recovered with zero production-owned descriptor delta. Swift-task delta is explicitly unavailable because the synchronous runner owns no tasks; process threads are not treated as a proxy.
- FINDING: Requested/effective buffers matched at 4096, 32768, and 262144 bytes. MTU 8500 with a 4096-byte send buffer produced 768 errno-40 `Message too long` refusals across the three family rows plus receive-queue drops; its maximum successful constrained datagram was 768 bytes. This is distinct from receiver overflow and makes 8500 unsuitable as a default solely because upstream uses it.
- RECOMMENDATION: Keep 1500 as the portable baseline; expose 1500...4096 only as an injectable candidate range when an end-to-end path is proven. Use measured requested buffers 32768...262144 bytes; 4096 remains fault injection. Loopback does not prove external fragmentation/path safety.
- GAPS: Physical iPhone remains `deferred-unavailable` under ADR-024. NAT64 is explicitly unavailable because no authorized deterministic local environment existed and route/Internet mutation was prohibited. Energy is unavailable from the unprivileged SPM harness; no sudo or `powermetrics` was used.
- VERIFICATION: The full Swift suite passed 474 tests in 40 suites (25 declared known ReluxNIOSSH-unavailable issues); focused matrix coverage is 87.10% regions, 88.17% functions, and 96.13% lines. Strict affected-file format lint and diff checks pass. Raw and analyzed task evidence is attached on the board.
- REVISION 3: A reviewer reproduced a post-parse parent swap that redirected the Foundation pathname write outside `.temp`. The production writer now uses no-follow `openat` traversal and an fd-bound atomic rename; production-entry tests reject both `.temp -> /tmp` cross-root escape and post-parse replacement. The 64-packet lower bound now applies a measured 4096-byte receiver-stall fault ceiling to 32-packet dual-stack halves. The rerun passed 477 tests; affected coverage is 85.84% regions, 89.11% functions, and 95.86% lines.

