@@ -5,6 +5,11 @@
 
 ## 2026-08-27
 
+### 0751 — Lifecycle observer allocation removed before classification (TASK-260715-135rr8)
+- ROOT CAUSE/FIX: `measureRealHEVLifecycle` retained every sample in an initially empty Swift `Array` after taking its baseline. The observer now reserves the exact bounded cycle count before the baseline snapshot. A production-call-site regression asserts capacity for 1000 samples, and the diagnostic entry accepts only 100/500/1000 cycles; malformed or wider values fail closed.
+- MEASUREMENT: Corrected exact-tree loopback probes ran 100/500/1000 real HEV cycles. Post-warmup net change was `+81,944 B` / `-212,992 B` / `-32,768 B`; maximum drawup was `98,328 B` / `65,536 B` / `65,536 B`; increase/equal/decrease transitions were `3/85/1`, `4/479/6`, and `7/977/5`. The prior late approximately 16 KiB jumps above cycle 1000 disappeared; the last 1000-cycle increase was cycle 481. Every sample restored live sessions, reads, and queues to zero; descriptors ended at 3 and threads at 8.
+- RULE: A fresh production-entry repeat proved 100 cycles insufficient: it stopped fail-closed on one `+65,536 B` increase and no release. The simplest repeatable gate therefore uses the next predeclared row, 500 cycles, after fixed 10-sample warmup. It permits a full plateau or a measured release only while maximum drawup stays within 256 KiB (1% of the upper 25 MiB target); late unreleased rise and a released-but-over-ceiling linear sawtooth fail closed. The earlier 2000-cycle/trailing-1000 rule measured observer allocation and is retired rather than widened further.
+
 ### 0732 — Extended lifecycle converges to a bounded HEV/runtime envelope (TASK-260715-135rr8)
 - INVESTIGATION: A bounded process-local 2000-cycle SwiftPM/loopback run captured every physical-footprint jump and 100-cycle segment. The sampler observed both rises and releases, including `-1,196,032 B` and `-1,130,496 B` segments; post-warmup net change was `-2,310,120 B`. Across the last 500 samples, net change was `-65,536 B` and range was `98,304 B`. Descriptors stayed `3`, threads stayed within `6...8`, and every post-cleanup HEV session, read, and queue count was zero. Boundary start/stop and HEV start/main-return counters were exactly one per cycle. Earlier 500- and 1000-cycle repeats still had late rises, proving neither duration alone established convergence.
 - RULE: The production evidence gate now requires at least 2000 samples (20× the original 100-cycle minimum), the existing fixed 10-sample allocator warmup, post-warmup and trailing 1000-sample maximum drawup no greater than `256 KiB` (1% of the upper 25 MiB provisional envelope), and either a trailing plateau or an observed post-warmup release. Maximum drawup measures each upward excursion from the running minimum, so a large release is not itself a failure. Raw evidence records every parameter, transition count, jump cycle, ownership counter, and sample. Positive plateau and bounded-oscillation tests plus unreleased late-rise and oversized-high-water negative tests bind the classifier; the original rise-plus-plateau negative remains.
